  "details": "Hello\n\nNot sure if this is a supposed behaviour or I mistake anything. I tried to create a layer for avator clothes toggle which consists of a series of animation nodes on condition. A minimal reproduction is shown in the screenshot.\n\nThe expected behaviour is that when bool_1 is true, show the hat (play hat_default animation), and if bool_1 is false, play the other hat animation, and then based on bool_2 play another animation right after, which is to show/hide the ears.\n\nHowever, in practice only the first animation node was working, and all nodes comes hierachically after the first active one have no effect. All the nodes were working if they were on separate layers tho.\n\nI was wondering if VRChat hard codes the way to render animation that it stops after the first matching animation node was found for each layer.\n\nAny help or information is appreciated, thanks!",
